      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. The prime factorization of 91 is:\n\n91 = 7 × 13\n\nNow, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors of a number. If a number n has the prime factorization n = p₁^a₁ × p₂^a₂ × ... × pₖ^aₖ, then the sum of all its divisors is given by:\n\nSum of divisors = (p₁^(a₁ + 1) - 1) / (p₁ - 1) × (p₂^(a₂ + 1) - 1) / (p₂ - 1) × ... × (pₖ^(aₖ + 1) - 1) / (pₖ - 1)\n\nFor 91, we have:\n\nSum of divisors = (7^(1 + 1) - 1) / (7 - 1) × (13^(1 + 1) - 1) / (13 - 1)\n                 = (7² - 1) / 6 × (13² - 1) / 12\n                 = (49 - 1) / 6 × (169 - 1) / 12\n                 = 48 / 6 × 168 / 12\n                 = 8 × 14\n                 = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
