      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization.\n\nThe prime factorization of 91 is 7 × 13, since 91 = 7 × 13.\n\nNext, we use the formula for the sum of divisors of a number. If a number n has the prime factorization n = p1^a1 × p2^a2 × ... × pk^ak, then the sum of its divisors is given by:\n\nSum = (p1^(a1 + 1) - 1)/(p1 - 1) × (p2^(a2 + 1) - 1)/(p2 - 1) × ... × (pk^(ak + 1) - 1)/(pk - 1)\n\nFor 91, this becomes:\n\nSum = (7^(1 + 1) - 1)/(7 - 1) × (13^(1 + 1) - 1)/(13 - 1)\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nSum = (7^2 - 1)/6 × (13^2 - 1)/12\n\nSum = (49 - 1)/6 × (169 - 1)/12\n\nSum = 48/6 × 168/12\n\nSum = 8 × 14\n\nSum = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
