    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can do this by dividing 91 by the smallest prime number, which is 2, and continuing with the next prime numbers until we can't divide evenly anymore.\n\n91 ÷ 2 = 45.5 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 3 = 30.33 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 5 = 18.2 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 7 = 13 (divisible)\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 91 is 7 × 13. Now, we can use this factorization to find the sum of all the positive divisors.\n\nThe formula for the sum of divisors of a number n = p₁^a₁ × p₂^a₂ × ... × pₖ^aₖ, where p₁, p₂, ..., pₖ are the prime factors and a₁, a₂, ..., aₖ are their respective exponents, is:\n\nSum = (p₁^(a₁ + 1) - 1) / (p₁ - 1) × (p₂^(a₂ + 1) - 1) / (p₂ - 1) × ... × (pₖ^(aₖ + 1) - 1) / (pₖ - 1)\n\nFor 91, the sum of divisors is:\n\nSum = (7^(1 + 1) - 1) / (7 - 1) × (13^(1 + 1) - 1) / (13 - 1)\nSum = (7^2 - 1) / 6 × (13^2 - 1) / 12\nSum = (49 - 1) / 6 × (169 - 1) / 12\nSum = 48 / 6 × 168 / 12\nSum = 8 × 14\nSum = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
